    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49932" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ūsĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		utor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>use</i> (ante- and postclass.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">domini usioni recipitur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 149, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae tibi usioni supererunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 38, 4</span></i>
			: usioni quod satis esset, Varr. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Non. 231, 6</span></i>: usionis
			gratiā, Scaevola ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 4, 1,
				17</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">usionis causā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					34, 2, 28</span></i>
			.—<i>Plur.</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Arn. 7, p. 238</span></i> dub.</div>
